<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Chinese version in the Garden of Stories (Liu Xiang)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation into Chinese (54 characters)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">History of Love (Qing Shi), Feng Menglong</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">c. 1628–1630</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the story included in its chapter on love between men</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Interpretation through the Tai languages (Wei Qingwen)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1981</span><span class="sg-chain-h">scholarly reading</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Version in written Thai (Zhengzhang Shangfang)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">scholarly reconstruction</span></li></ul></section>
